{% comment %}
  The product's own selling plans, as cards, with nothing typed in.

  The supply block asks for a plan id, an interval, a price and a saving per
  card. That is right for NanoGreens, where each option is merchandised — gifts,
  an add-on, a per-serving figure — and wrong for a template assigned to
  twenty-eight products, because every one of those four values differs per
  product and a typed one would be silently wrong on all but the product it was
  typed for.

  So this block types none of them. It walks the current variant's selling plan
  allocations and renders a card per plan: name from the plan, price from the
  allocation, saving computed against the allocation's own compare-at. A product
  with no plans renders nothing, which is what makes the block safe to leave in
  the template for the one-time-only products.

  Prices are the real charge, undivided. The supply block normalises every card
  to a 4-week rate so a quarterly plan can be compared against a monthly one;
  that only works because the interval is typed in there, and there is no
  reliable interval to read off a selling plan. Showing the actual amount is the
  honest alternative, and the plan name carries the cadence — Loop writes
  "Delivered every month" — so the card still says how often it charges.

  Cards emit the same data-cwc-offer attributes the supply cards do and share
  their radio group name, so the sticky bar's plan menu, the add-to-cart form
  and the price refresh all treat the two interchangeably. The two blocks are
  alternatives, not companions: use this one or that one, not both.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the purchase_plans block.
  - product {Object} - product being sold.
  - current_variant {Object} - variant whose allocations are rendered.
  - section_id {String} - scopes the radio group name to this section.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-purchase-plans__block',
    block: block,
    product: product,
    current_variant: current_variant,
    section_id: section.id
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign allocations = current_variant.selling_plan_allocations
  assign savings_style = block.settings.savings_style | default: 'percent'
  assign default_plan = block.settings.default_plan | default: 'best_value'

  comment
    Which card carries the badge and, unless the block says otherwise, the
    initial selection. Decided by the deepest discount rather than by position,
    because the plan order Shopify returns is the order they were created in and
    has nothing to do with which is the better deal.

    Held as an id, not an index: the loop below runs over the same collection,
    so comparing ids is enough and there is no counter to keep in step.
  endcomment
  assign best_plan_id = 0
  assign best_discount = 0

  for allocation in allocations
    assign alloc_compare = allocation.compare_at_price | default: 0
    if alloc_compare > allocation.price
      assign alloc_discount = alloc_compare | minus: allocation.price | times: 10000 | divided_by: alloc_compare
      if alloc_discount > best_discount
        assign best_discount = alloc_discount
        assign best_plan_id = allocation.selling_plan.id
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Nothing is discounted — a flat subscription. The badge then has no deal to
    point at, so it falls to the first plan only when it is being used as the
    default marker rather than as a "best value" claim.
  endcomment
  if best_plan_id == 0 and allocations.size > 0
    assign best_plan_id = allocations.first.selling_plan.id
  endif
-%}

{%- if allocations.size > 0 -%}
  <div {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {% if block.settings.group_label != blank %}
      <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__label">{{ block.settings.group_label }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    {%- comment -%}
      "Nothing pre-selected" has to be announced, not just left undone: the
      script selects the first card when it finds none selected, which would
      quietly undo the setting on the next line.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div
      class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offers"
      data-cwc-offers
      {% if default_plan == 'none' %}
        data-cwc-no-autoselect
      {% endif %}
    >
      {%- assign default_taken = false -%}

      {%- for allocation in allocations -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign plan = allocation.selling_plan
          assign plan_price = allocation.price
          assign plan_compare = allocation.compare_at_price | default: 0

          assign has_saving = false
          if plan_compare > plan_price
            assign has_saving = true
            assign saving_amount = plan_compare | minus: plan_price
            assign saving_percent = saving_amount | times: 100 | divided_by: plan_compare
          endif

          assign is_best = false
          if plan.id == best_plan_id
            assign is_best = true
          endif

          comment
            One card starts selected, and only one. "None" is deliberately
            allowed: a shopper who must pick is a shopper who read the options,
            and on a two-card product that is a fair trade for the extra click.
          endcomment
          assign is_selected = false
          if default_taken == false
            case default_plan
              when 'best_value'
                if is_best
                  assign is_selected = true
                endif
              when 'first'
                if forloop.first
                  assign is_selected = true
                endif
            endcase
          endif
          if is_selected
            assign default_taken = true
          endif

          comment
            The badge is a claim about price, so it is withheld when no plan is
            discounted — labelling the only plan "Best value" says nothing.
          endcomment
          assign show_badge = false
          if block.settings.best_value_badge != blank and is_best and best_discount > 0 and allocations.size > 1
            assign show_badge = true
          endif

          assign save_label = ''
          if has_saving
            case savings_style
              when 'percent'
                assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_percent | append: '%'
              when 'amount'
                assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_amount | money
              when 'both'
                assign save_label = 'Save ' | append: saving_percent | append: '% · ' | append: saving_amount | money
            endcase
          endif
        -%}

        <label
          class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer{% if is_selected %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer--selected{% endif %}"
          data-cwc-offer
          {%- comment -%}
            Marks the card as generated from the product's own plans. The script
            hides a card whose plan the selected variant cannot be bought on, and
            that is only safe to do for cards it generated: a supply card with a
            mistyped plan id would otherwise vanish instead of falling back to
            its typed prices, which is a far harder mistake to spot.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          data-cwc-offer-auto
          data-cwc-offer-plan="{{ plan.id }}"
          data-cwc-offer-quantity="1"
          data-cwc-offer-variant="{{ current_variant.id }}"
          data-cwc-offer-name="{{ plan.name | escape }}"
          data-cwc-offer-sub="{{ save_label | escape }}"
        >
          {% if show_badge %}
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-badge">{{ block.settings.best_value_badge }}</span>
          {% endif %}

          <input
            type="radio"
            name="cwc_supply_{{ section_id }}"
            class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-input"
            value="{{ block.id }}-{{ plan.id }}"
            {% if is_selected %}
              checked
            {% endif %}
          >

          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-radio" aria-hidden="true"></span>

          <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-body">
            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-name">
              {{ plan.name }}
              {% if save_label != blank %}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-save{% unless is_selected %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-save--dim{% endunless %}">
                  {{ save_label }}
                </span>
              {% endif %}
            </span>

            {% if block.settings.show_plan_description and plan.description != blank %}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-description">{{ plan.description }}</span>
            {% endif %}

            <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-price">
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-now" data-cwc-offer-now>{{ plan_price | money }}</span>
              {% if has_saving %}
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-was" data-cwc-offer-was>{{ plan_compare | money }}</span>
              {% endif %}
            </span>

            {%- comment -%}
              The perks strip is typed copy that applies to every plan on every
              product the template serves, so it says what subscribing means
              rather than what this plan costs. Left blank it does not render and
              the card has no open state at all.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if block.settings.perks != blank -%}
              <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details" data-cwc-offer-details>
                <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-details-inner">
                  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__offer-perks cwc-rte">{{ block.settings.perks }}</span>
                </span>
              </span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </span>
        </label>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
